# Lecture template app

Students upload notes, textbooks, or slides. We generate a **fill-in lecture template**, not completed notes and not homework answers.

## Stack

- Frontend: React in `frontend/`
- Backend: Python + FastAPI in `backend/`
- Database: PostgreSQL
- AI: NVIDIA Nemotron via the OpenAI-compatible API (`https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1`)
- Nemotron is text-only. Never send images to it.

## Scope

- In scope: ingest source material, extract text, generate templates with toggles (definitions, diagrams, code blocks; more filled vs more blank).
- Out of scope: homework Q&A, solving problems, writing full answers, chatting over a notes folder.
- Show a disclaimer that generated templates may miss topics.

## Ingest

1. Extract native PDF text first (PyMuPDF).
2. OCR with Tesseract only when a page has almost no extractable text, or the upload is an image.
3. Handwriting is later; do not build a handwriting path unless asked.

## Secrets

Never commit `.env`, API keys, or database URLs. Use `.env.example` with `NVIDIA_API_KEY` and `DATABASE_URL` only.
